{"id":"h130","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"When focused on a star, the distance of the eye lens of a simple telescope from the objective lens is 82 cm. The focal length of the eye lens is 2.0 cm. To see a certain tree (with the same eye accommodation), the eye lens must be drawn out 1.0 cm. Find the distance of the tree from the telescope.\nIs the correct answer \"64.8 meters\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct answer of 64.8 m is right.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"For a telescope focused on a distant star, the lens separation equals f₀ + f_e.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"With separation 82 cm and f_e = 2 cm, the objective focal length is 80 cm.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Same eye accommodation means the final virtual image stays at infinity, so the intermediate image lies at the eyepiece focal point.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"After drawing the eyepiece out 1 cm, the separation is 83 cm so the intermediate image is 81 cm from the objective.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The lens equation with f = 80 cm and v = 81 cm gives an object distance of 6480 cm = 64.8 m.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The wording 'same eye accommodation' is slightly ambiguous and could mean the eye focuses at another fixed distance.","confidence":0.2,"lean":-1,"theta":0.3142,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The relaxed-eye reading is the standard interpretation and is consistent with the given numbers.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The conditions together give a unique object distance of 64.8 m.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"s